{
  "name": "Shadow AI & Vendor Approval Gate with RelayShield",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Shadow AI & Vendor Approval Gate with RelayShield\n\n### How it works\nRuns when a new SaaS vendor or AI-tool request is submitted (form or ITSM ticket) via this workflow's webhook. Branches on `request_type`: a plain SaaS request runs three checks (supply chain risk, public-repo secret exposure, OAuth/token exposure). An AI-tool request runs those plus `mcp-registry-risk` — typosquat domains, known-malicious IOCs, newly-registered MCP server domains. Either path alerts Slack, logs to Notion, and emails the requester an approve/pending-review outcome. Clean results are logged too, so every request is auditable.\n\n### Setup steps\n- Point your intake form or ITSM system at this workflow's webhook, posting `{ request_type: \"saas\"|\"ai_tool\", requester_name, requester_email, department, vendor_name, vendor_domain, server_url }` (`server_url`/`package_name` only for `ai_tool`)\n- Add your RelayShield API credential to the 4 custom RelayShield nodes. The Secret Scan and MCP Registry Risk checks use HTTP Request nodes with a Header Auth credential instead (header `X-RS-API-KEY`, value = your API key) — those two operations aren't in the community node's operation list yet\n- Set `notionVendorGateDbId` and `slackSecurityChannelId` in your n8n variables\n- Connect and authorize the Gmail and Slack credentials\n\n### Why the OAuth check runs against the requester, not the vendor\nIt checks the *requesting employee's* email, not the vendor's — the real question at approval time is whether the person about to grant this tool OAuth access already shows signs of compromised credentials. That's the person whose authority the integration would inherit.\n\n### Customization\nAdd more RelayShield checks (ransomware risk, identity graph) to broaden coverage, or adjust alert routing to match your escalation process.",
        "height": 1000,
        "width": 560,
        "color": 5
      },
      "id": "c4d5e6f7-0000-0000-0000-000000000000",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -1000,
        0
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "httpMethod": "POST",
        "path": "vendor-tool-request",
        "responseMode": "onReceived",
        "responseData": "firstEntryJson",
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "c4d5e6f7-0001-0001-0001-000000000001",
      "name": "Vendor/AI-Tool Request Webhook",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.webhook",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        0,
        770
      ],
      "webhookId": "relayshield-vendor-gate-001",
      "notes": "Receives an HTTP POST from your intake form or ITSM system for a new vendor/tool request. Expected payload: { \"request_type\": \"saas\" or \"ai_tool\", \"requester_name\": \"Jane Doe\", \"requester_email\": \"jane@company.com\", \"department\": \"Engineering\", \"vendor_name\": \"Acme Corp\", \"vendor_domain\": \"acme.com\", \"server_url\": \"https://mcp.acme.com/sse\" }. server_url (or package_name) only applies to ai_tool requests."
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "conditions": {
          "options": {
            "caseSensitive": true,
            "leftValue": "",
            "typeValidation": "strict"
          },
          "conditions": [
            {
              "id": "branch-cond-001",
              "leftValue": "={{ $json.request_type }}",
              "rightValue": "ai_tool",
              "operator": {
                "type": "string",
                "operation": "equals"
              }
            }
          ],
          "combinator": "and"
        }
      },
      "id": "c4d5e6f7-0002-0002-0002-000000000002",
      "name": "Is AI-Tool Request?",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.if",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        280,
        770
      ],
      "notes": "Branches on request_type. AI-tool requests (true output) get the additional mcp-registry-risk check; plain SaaS vendor requests (false output) get the original three checks."
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "operation": "supplyChain",
        "vendorDomains": "={{ $('Vendor/AI-Tool Request Webhook').item.json.vendor_domain }}",
        "vendorEmails": ""
      },
      "id": "c4d5e6f7-0003-0003-0003-000000000003",
      "name": "RelayShield - Supply Chain Risk (SaaS)",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-relayshield.relayShield",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        560,
        1060
      ],
      "credentials": {
        "relayShieldApi": {
          "id": "1",
          "name": "RelayShield API"
        }
      },
      "notes": "Checks the vendor domain for breach and infostealer exposure — returns a per-domain risk score (CRITICAL/HIGH/MEDIUM/LOW)."
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "method": "POST",
        "url": "https://api.relayshield.net/v1/metered/secret-scan",
        "sendBody": true,
        "specifyBody": "json",
        "jsonBody": "={{ JSON.stringify({ vendor_domains: [ $('Vendor/AI-Tool Request Webhook').item.json.vendor_domain ] }) }}",
        "sendHeaders": true,
        "headerParameters": {
          "parameters": [
            {
              "name": "Content-Type",
              "value": "application/json"
            }
          ]
        },
        "authentication": "genericCredentialType",
        "genericAuthType": "httpHeaderAuth",
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "c4d5e6f7-0004-0004-0004-000000000004",
      "name": "RelayShield - Secret Scan (SaaS)",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "typeVersion": 4.2,
      "position": [
        560,
        1300
      ],
      "credentials": {
        "httpHeaderAuth": {
          "id": "5",
          "name": "RelayShield API Key (Header Auth)"
        }
      },
      "notes": "Checks public GitHub repos for secrets exposed alongside the vendor domain. Not yet in the n8n-nodes-relayshield package's operation list — called directly via HTTP Request with an X-RS-API-KEY header credential."
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "operation": "oauthWatchlist",
        "email": "={{ $('Vendor/AI-Tool Request Webhook').item.json.requester_email }}"
      },
      "id": "c4d5e6f7-0005-0005-0005-000000000005",
      "name": "RelayShield - OAuth Watchlist (SaaS)",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-relayshield.relayShield",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        560,
        1540
      ],
      "credentials": {
        "relayShieldApi": {
          "id": "1",
          "name": "RelayShield API"
        }
      },
      "notes": "Checks the requesting employee's email for OAuth/token exposure — this is the person who would grant the new tool access, not the vendor."
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "conditions": {
          "options": {
            "caseSensitive": true,
            "leftValue": "",
            "typeValidation": "strict"
          },
          "conditions": [
            {
              "id": "saas-cond-001",
              "leftValue": "={{ $('RelayShield - Supply Chain Risk (SaaS)').item.json.data.highest_risk }}",
              "rightValue": "CRITICAL",
              "operator": {
                "type": "string",
                "operation": "equals"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "saas-cond-002",
              "leftValue": "={{ $('RelayShield - Supply Chain Risk (SaaS)').item.json.data.highest_risk }}",
              "rightValue": "HIGH",
              "operator": {
                "type": "string",
                "operation": "equals"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "saas-cond-003",
              "leftValue": "={{ $('RelayShield - Secret Scan (SaaS)').item.json.data.found }}",
              "rightValue": true,
              "operator": {
                "type": "boolean",
                "operation": "true"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "saas-cond-004",
              "leftValue": "={{ $('RelayShield - OAuth Watchlist (SaaS)').item.json.data.matched }}",
              "rightValue": true,
              "operator": {
                "type": "boolean",
                "operation": "true"
              }
            }
          ],
          "combinator": "or"
        }
      },
      "id": "c4d5e6f7-0006-0006-0006-000000000006",
      "name": "Any SaaS Risk Found?",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.if",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        840,
        1300
      ],
      "notes": "Flags the request if the vendor domain shows critical/high supply-chain risk, has exposed secrets in public repos, or the requester's own account shows OAuth/token exposure."
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "operation": "supplyChain",
        "vendorDomains": "={{ $('Vendor/AI-Tool Request Webhook').item.json.vendor_domain }}",
        "vendorEmails": ""
      },
      "id": "c4d5e6f7-0007-0007-0007-000000000007",
      "name": "RelayShield - Supply Chain Risk (AI Tool)",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-relayshield.relayShield",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        560,
        0
      ],
      "credentials": {
        "relayShieldApi": {
          "id": "1",
          "name": "RelayShield API"
        }
      },
      "notes": "Checks the AI tool publisher's domain for breach and infostealer exposure, same as the SaaS path. Leave vendor_domain blank on the request if the publisher domain isn't known — the check will report no findings rather than fail."
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "method": "POST",
        "url": "https://api.relayshield.net/v1/metered/secret-scan",
        "sendBody": true,
        "specifyBody": "json",
        "jsonBody": "={{ JSON.stringify({ vendor_domains: [ $('Vendor/AI-Tool Request Webhook').item.json.vendor_domain ] }) }}",
        "sendHeaders": true,
        "headerParameters": {
          "parameters": [
            {
              "name": "Content-Type",
              "value": "application/json"
            }
          ]
        },
        "authentication": "genericCredentialType",
        "genericAuthType": "httpHeaderAuth",
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "c4d5e6f7-0008-0008-0008-000000000008",
      "name": "RelayShield - Secret Scan (AI Tool)",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "typeVersion": 4.2,
      "position": [
        560,
        240
